## What needs human review before publish

### Substantive behavior changes — read these carefully

1. **`src/cli/init/writeMcpEntry/index.ts`** — full rewrite from one-key
   write to four-branch migration. The CLI install path is the cold-start
   surface for new users; if this has a bug, every fresh install breaks.
   Test count went 9 → 16; verify the four branches are all covered.
2. **`src/service/install/provisionBrain/index.ts`** — `buildBrainMcpStep`
   migration logic. Same three branches as writeMcpEntry, but lives
   on the planner side. The MCP-tool path through `aide_init`.
3. **`src/tools/brain/index.ts`** + **`composeInstructions/index.ts`** —
   the new `aide_brain` orchestrator and its instruction composer.
   Defensive impossible-state collapse worth a sanity check.
4. **`src/service/brainBackends/index.ts`** — the registry. Single
   matcher table. POSIX + Windows shapes for the obsidian matcher.
5. **`src/service/buildBrainState/index.ts`** — lifted from tools/info
   to service. New wired-but-unrecognized branch. Defensive narrowing
   of `command` field.
6. **`src/tools/validate/index.ts`** — small but it ships to every
   downstream project. The gate to intent/research only is correct
   per `plan-aide.md` but it does change behavior. Isolated commit so
   it can be reverted independently.

